From: Tobias Fischer <info@tobiasfischer.info>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:00:25 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Download model weights on first use

The weights (about 4 GB in total, SAM alone 2.5 GB) were only fetched by
install.py. A missing file made a tool fail with a bare exception, or,
for SAM, silently removed the SAM buttons.

source/ModelWeights.py adds ensureModel(name): if the file is not in the
models folder it asks, then downloads it from taglab.isti.cnr.it/models
(the URLs install.py uses) with a Qt progress dialog that can be cancelled.
The file is written as *.part and renamed when complete, so an interrupted
download is never mistaken for a finished one. It returns None when the
user declines, cancels or the download fails (the user has been told),
and the tools just stop.

Used by the 4-clicks (DEXTR), RITM, SAM and interactive SAM tools, the
automatic classifiers (*.net) and the base network of the DeepLab
training. SAM is now offered whenever segment_anything is installed,
instead of only when the weights were already present, so the download
can be offered where the user needs it. Also restores the wait cursor
when RITM cannot load its network.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
